Package: bibliograph-happyview
Version: @VERSION@
Section: web
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>
Homepage: https://biblio.livtet.olamaelcu.net
Depends: libc6, libssl3 | libssl3t64, libgcc-s1, zlib1g, python3, postgresql-client, adduser, ca-certificates
Recommends: postgresql
Description: HappyView activity plane for Bibliograph
 HappyView indexes atproto activity records and serves the activity XRPC
 queries and write procedures for the Bibliograph appview. It runs as its own
 service on 127.0.0.1:3000; the SvelteKit application (bibliograph) proxies
 /xrpc to it and is the only public origin.
 .
 The binary, its Postgres migrations and the built dashboard are extracted
 from the pinned container image and installed under
 /usr/lib/bibliograph-happyview. No Node.js or container runtime is needed on
 the host.
 .
 A oneshot unit uploads this package's lexicons, query scripts and write
 procedures on install and writes the activity indexes. It bootstraps an
 administrative user and key first (in
 /etc/bibliograph/happyview-admin.key), because a fresh HappyView has no
 credentials with which to accept an upload.
 .
 Configuration lives in /etc/bibliograph/happyview.env. DATABASE_URL must name
 a role whose default search_path is "happyview, public"; db-init.sql in
 /usr/share/bibliograph-happyview creates that role and schema, and must be run
 once as a Postgres superuser.
